{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_0197Rj4XQDUwqwoQJxZjVJmW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The acceptance criteria for US-006 says to use Caddy programmatically via `caddy.Load()`. However, looking at go.mod, Caddy is not in the dependencies yet. Let me think about how to implement this.\n\nThe AC says:\n1. Reverse proxy listens on ports 80 and 443\n2. Each registered site gets tls internal (Caddy's built-in local CA) and reverse_proxy to its upstream\n3. Caddy config is built programmatically via caddy.Load() — no Caddyfile on disk\n4. Reload(table) rebuilds and hot-reloads config from the current routing table\n\n\n5. Integration test: start proxy on high ports, register a route, verify HTTPS request reaches a test HTTP server\n\nI know Caddy as a library brings in a substantial dependency tree, but the PRD specifically requires it. The main entry point is `github.com/caddyserver/caddy/v2` with its `caddy.Load()` function that accepts JSON configuration. I'll need to add the Caddy dependency, create a Server struct in `internal/proxy/proxy.go`, and build out the implementation.\n\nNow I'm checking if there's existing documentation or a plan file that might clarify the requirements further.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6446,"cache_read_input_tokens":21657,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6446},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b3e2ec84-c6d0-495a-acfd-c629e33a07ba","uuid":"04536c1b-979c-40c7-abe7-b994b91b9db6"}
