{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DiXLd5MmZLQpSidbf9sPyg","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→## Codebase Patterns\n     2→- Use `gopkg.in/yaml.v3` for YAML marshaling/unmarshaling\n     3→- Pre-commit hook runs `golangci-lint` — must use `_ =` for intentionally ignored error returns (errcheck)\n     4→- Atomic file writes: use `os.CreateTemp` + `os.Rename` pattern\n     5→- Module path: `github.com/vansdevcode/worktree-manager`\n     6→- Existing CLI is `cmd/wtm/`, new devtree CLI goes in `cmd/devtree/`\n     7→- Config dir convention: `~/.config/devtree/` for routing state files\n     8→- DNS package uses `mdns` import alias for `github.com/miekg/dns` to avoid collision with package name\n     9→- miekg/dns `Server.NotifyStartedFunc` callback signals when server is ready to accept connections\n    10→- Caddy programmatic config: build JSON as `map[string]any`, marshal, pass to `caddy.Load(data, true)`\n    11→- Import `_ \"github.com/caddyserver/caddy/v2/modules/standard\"` to register all standard Caddy modules\n    12→- TLS test clients must set `ServerName` in `tls.Config` to match the domain (SNI), not the IP address\n    13→- Daemon pattern: hidden `daemon` subcommand runs foreground; `start` launches it detached via `exec.Command` + `Setsid`\n    14→- PID file lifecycle: write on start, check with signal 0, remove on stop/SIGTERM cleanup\n    15→- Platform-specific code uses build tags in separate files (e.g., `daemon_unix.go` with `//go:build !windows`)\n    16→- Unix socket paths limited to ~104 chars on macOS; use `/tmp` for test sockets, not `t.TempDir()`\n    17→\n    18→## 2026-03-05 - US-001\n    19→- Implemented `internal/routing` package with routing table YAML state file\n    20→- Types: `Table` (holds `Sites` map), `Site` (Upstream string, Meta map)\n    21→- Functions: `Load(path)`, `Save(path, table)` with atomic write (temp + rename)\n    22→- Methods: `Register`, `Unregister`, `Get`, `List` (sorted alphabetically)\n    23→- Files changed: `internal/routing/routing.go`, `internal/routing/routing_test.go`\n    24→- **Learnings for future iterations:**\n    25→  - golangci-lint errcheck requires `_ =` prefix for intentionally ignored error returns in cleanup paths\n    26→  - `gopkg.in/yaml.v3` is already in go.sum, no need to `go get` it\n    27→  - YAML unmarshal into a struct with nil map needs a nil check after unmarshal\n    28→---\n    29→\n    30→## 2026-03-05 - US-002\n    31→- Implemented `devtree register <domain> --port <port>` CLI command\n    32→- Created `cmd/devtree/` package with `main.go`, `root.go`, `register.go`\n    33→- Register loads routes.yaml, calls `table.Register()`, saves atomically, prints confirmation\n    34→- Supports `--meta key=value` flags (repeatable) for arbitrary metadata\n    35→- Attempts Unix socket reload (best-effort, silently ignored if daemon not running)\n    36→- Files changed: `cmd/devtree/main.go`, `cmd/devtree/root.go`, `cmd/devtree/register.go`\n    37→- **Learnings for future iterations:**\n    38→  - `defer conn.Close()` must be `defer func() { _ = conn.Close() }()` for errcheck\n    39→  - devtree CLI uses cobra, same as wtm CLI but in separate `cmd/devtree/` package\n    40→  - `DefaultRoutesPath()` and `DefaultSocketPath()` are in `root.go` for reuse by other subcommands\n    41→---\n    42→\n    43→## 2026-03-05 - US-003\n    44→- Implemented `devtree unregister <domain>` CLI command\n    45→- Created `cmd/devtree/unregister.go` with `runUnregister` function\n    46→- Loads routes.yaml, calls `table.Unregister()` (returns error if domain not found), saves atomically, prints confirmation\n    47→- Reuses `sendReload()` from register.go for Unix socket reload\n    48→- Added `unregisterCmd` to root command in `root.go`\n    49→- Files changed: `cmd/devtree/unregister.go` (new), `cmd/devtree/root.go` (modified)\n    50→- **Learnings for future iterations:**\n    51→  - `table.Unregister()` already returns an error for non-existent domains, so cobra's `RunE` propagates it as a non-zero exit\n    52→  - `sendReload()` is already defined in `register.go` and available package-wide — no need to duplicate\n    53→---\n    54→\n    55→## 2026-03-05 - US-004\n    56→- Implemented `devtree list` CLI command\n    57→- Created `cmd/devtree/list.go` with tabwriter-based table output\n    58→- Prints \"No routes registered\" when table is empty\n    59→- Output sorted alphabetically by domain (uses `table.List()` which already sorts)\n    60→- Meta displayed as comma-separated key=value pairs\n    61→- Files changed: `cmd/devtree/list.go` (new), `cmd/devtree/root.go` (modified)\n    62→- **Learnings for future iterations:**\n    63→  - `text/tabwriter` works well for CLI table output with tab-separated columns\n    64→  - `table.List()` already returns sites sorted alphabetically — no extra sorting needed in the command\n    65→---\n    66→\n    67→## 2026-03-05 - US-005\n    68→- Implemented `internal/dns` package with embedded DNS server\n    69→- `Server` struct wraps UDP and TCP `miekg/dns` servers\n    70→- `handler.ServeDNS` resolves `*.test` A queries to 127.0.0.1, all others get NXDOMAIN\n    71→- Functions: `New(addr)`, `Start()` (blocks until ready), `Stop()`\n    72→- Files changed: `internal/dns/dns.go` (new), `internal/dns/dns_test.go` (new), `go.mod`, `go.sum`\n    73→- 6 tests: UDP/TCP resolution, subdomains, NXDOMAIN for non-.test, NXDOMAIN for non-A queries, case insensitivity\n    74→- **Learnings for future iterations:**\n    75→  - Use `mdns` as import alias for `github.com/miekg/dns` to avoid package name collision\n    76→  - miekg/dns doesn't support port 0; tests must find a free port first via `net.ListenUDP`, then close and pass to `New()`\n    77→  - `Server.NotifyStartedFunc` is the reliable way to wait for server readiness before sending queries\n    78→  - DNS names are FQDN with trailing dot — match with `strings.HasSuffix(name, \".test.\")`\n    79→---